From: MyszkinPL <211237936+MyszkinPL@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: sunxi: restart, and power off, through the SoC watchdog before PSCI

On the Yandex Station 1 (A64, vendor ATF + AR100 SCP firmware) PSCI
SYSTEM_RESET is forwarded to the SCP, and with the SCP alive the board
can end up hung after it (STM32 boot animation, no U-Boot/Android, the
SoC watchdog never fires) until power is removed. A reset through the
SoC watchdog has always worked. PSCI registers its restart handler at
priority 129 (drivers/firmware/psci/psci.c), above the 128 used here,
so reboot and panic took the PSCI path. Use 192 so the watchdog goes
first; PSCI stays as the fallback, which sunxi_wdt_restart() never
returns to.

PSCI SYSTEM_OFF on that board makes the SCP switch every PMIC rail off
(AXP803 reg 0x32 := 0x80); with no battery and no power key the board
stays dead until it is unplugged. On that board only (by its compatible),
power-off restarts through the watchdog too, ahead of PSCI's handler.

Signed-off-by: MyszkinPL <211237936+MyszkinPL@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/watchdog/sunxi_wdt.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/sunxi_wdt.c
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@
 #include <linux/moduleparam.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
+#include <linux/reboot.h>
 #include <linux/types.h>
 #include <linux/watchdog.h>
 
@@ -278,6 +279,19 @@
 	.wdt_key_val = 0x16aa0000,
 };
 
+/*
+ * Power-off on the Yandex Station 1: PSCI SYSTEM_OFF makes the vendor SCP
+ * firmware switch every PMIC rail off, and there is no battery and no key
+ * to come back with — only unplugging. Restart through the watchdog
+ * instead, ahead of PSCI's handler.
+ */
+static int sunxi_wdt_power_off(struct sys_off_data *data)
+{
+	struct sunxi_wdt_dev *sunxi_wdt = data->cb_data;
+
+	return sunxi_wdt_restart(&sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev, 0, NULL);
+}
+
 static const struct of_device_id sunxi_wdt_dt_ids[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "allwinner,sun4i-a10-wdt", .data = &sun4i_wdt_reg },
 	{ .compatible = "allwinner,sun6i-a31-wdt", .data = &sun6i_wdt_reg },
@@ -315,7 +329,12 @@
 
 	watchdog_init_timeout(&sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev, timeout, dev);
 	watchdog_set_nowayout(&sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev, nowayout);
-	watchdog_set_restart_priority(&sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev, 128);
+	/*
+	 * Above PSCI (129): on the Yandex Station 1 PSCI SYSTEM_RESET goes
+	 * to the vendor SCP firmware and can leave the board hung, while a
+	 * watchdog reset always reboots cleanly.
+	 */
+	watchdog_set_restart_priority(&sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev, 192);
 
 	watchdog_set_drvdata(&sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev, sunxi_wdt);
 
@@ -335,6 +354,14 @@
 	err = devm_watchdog_register_device(dev, &sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev);
 	if (unlikely(err))
 		return err;
+
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("yandex,station-tulip-d1")) {
+		err = devm_register_sys_off_handler(dev, SYS_OFF_MODE_POWER_OFF,
+						    SYS_OFF_PRIO_FIRMWARE + 1,
+						    sunxi_wdt_power_off, sunxi_wdt);
+		if (err)
+			return err;
+	}
 
 	dev_info(dev, "Watchdog enabled (timeout=%d sec, nowayout=%d)",
 		 sunxi_wdt->wdt_dev.timeout, nowayout);
